      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.12,
          "end": 2.88,
          "en": "-: So let's understand what happens when you create a branch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.88,
          "end": 4.53,
          "en": "So let's say, you have just done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.53,
          "end": 6.93,
          "en": "the Git registration on the working directory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.93,
          "end": 8.82,
          "en": "Now at this point, what happens is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 8.82,
          "end": 11.91,
          "en": "you get a different area inside your working directory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.91,
          "end": 14.88,
          "en": "which is called your Git, right .git folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.88,
          "end": 17.01,
          "en": "Now basically, whenever you do your commits,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.01,
          "end": 18.39,
          "en": "of course, you have to do this commits",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 18.39,
          "end": 19.44,
          "en": "in some branch, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 19.44,
          "end": 21.96,
          "en": "And by default, when you say git in it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 21.96,
          "end": 23.76,
          "en": "it creates a master branch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 23.76,
          "end": 25.08,
          "en": "So let's say, in our case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 25.08,
          "end": 26.55,
          "en": "we are creating a main branch, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 26.55,
          "end": 29.4,
          "en": "So default for us is main branch, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 29.4,
          "end": 32.46,
          "en": "Now, every time you basically do the commit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 32.46,
          "end": 34.38,
          "en": "so let's say when you do the first commit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 34.38,
          "end": 37.38,
          "en": "what Git does is, it creates something called a snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 37.38,
          "end": 40.08,
          "en": "So it'll take a snapshot of your files, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 40.08,
          "end": 42.75,
          "en": "And then it'll give it its own commit number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 42.75,
          "end": 44.79,
          "en": "That's your checksum, basically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 44.79,
          "end": 47.31,
          "en": "We have seen the hexacode values, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 47.31,
          "end": 48.75,
          "en": "So that's your checksum.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 48.75,
          "end": 51.09,
          "en": "And then, there's one more thing called pointer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 51.09,
          "end": 53.04,
          "en": "Now how the pointer looks like, let me show you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 53.04,
          "end": 54.75,
          "en": "So if you say git log,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 54.75,
          "end": 55.59,
          "en": "and when you say enter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 55.59,
          "end": 57.9,
          "en": "remember this, we have seen this thing before?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 57.9,
          "end": 59.55,
          "en": "There's something called, head.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 59.55,
          "end": 62.55,
          "en": "So at this point it is showing me a feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 62.55,
          "end": 64.05,
          "en": "Because we are into feature branch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 64.05,
          "end": 66.69,
          "en": "What I will do is, let me just switch to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 66.69,
          "end": 69.66,
          "en": "I would say git switch main.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 69.66,
          "end": 72.42,
          "en": "And now if I do the same command again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 72.42,
          "end": 74.55,
          "en": "you can see it says, head is towards main.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 74.55,
          "end": 76.74,
          "en": "Let's say we don't have a feature branch at this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 76.74,
          "end": 79.5,
          "en": "we only have main branch and then the header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 79.5,
          "end": 81,
          "en": "So that's your main pointer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 81,
          "end": 83.67,
          "en": "So it is pointing to the main branch, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 83.67,
          "end": 87.45,
          "en": "And main is basically pointing to your, to your commit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 87.45,
          "end": 90.03,
          "en": "Now this recent commit is this one, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 90.03,
          "end": 91.17,
          "en": "Now, let's say next time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 91.17,
          "end": 92.66,
          "en": "you are doing one more commit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 92.66,
          "end": 94.08,
          "en": "in the same branch, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 94.08,
          "end": 96.18,
          "en": "So what it will do is, it will take a snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 96.18,
          "end": 97.62,
          "en": "Now, in this snapshot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 97.62,
          "end": 99.93,
          "en": "basically, you will have those files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 99.93,
          "end": 101.72999999999999,
          "en": "which have been changed, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 101.72999999999999,
          "end": 103.59,
          "en": "So it will not simply copy every file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 103.59,
          "end": 106.2,
          "en": "it will copy those files which have been changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 106.2,
          "end": 108.297,
          "en": "Now you have a previous commit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
